## 1. scaffold a real no-mistakes brief with bin/fm-brief.sh
fm-brief rc=0
--- brief lines carrying the recovery playbook:
136:1. Read the run head from `no-mistakes axi status`: `branch_sync.pipeline.current_head`, or `head_sha` only when that is empty. Find the gate worktree whose HEAD is that run head in `git -C "$(git remote get-url no-mistakes)" worktree list` and run `git fetch <that worktree path> HEAD:refs/heads/archive/<your branch>`. Only when a ref in `git ls-remote no-mistakes` points at the run head may you fetch from the store instead: fetch by that ref name, such as the recover ref `refs/no-mistakes/recover/<run id>`, or by the full 40-character sha; an abbreviated sha is read as a ref name and always fails.
140:Before you conclude anything, run `for r in ~/.no-mistakes/repos/*.git; do git -C "$r" cat-file -e <run head>^{commit} 2>/dev/null && echo "$r holds it"; git -C "$r" for-each-ref --format="$r %(refname)" --contains <run head> 2>/dev/null; done`, fetch a ref match by its ref name from that store, and fetch from a store that holds the head with no ref by the full 40-character sha.
